          "date": "2026-10-22 02:14:09.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-21013 lnet: do not spin on a forced push in flight",
        "message": "LU-21013 lnet: do not spin on a forced push in flight\n\nA peer can get LNET_PEER_FORCE_PUSH while its push is in flight.\nThen lnet_discovery can spin until the push ACK arrives or times\nout (150 s). The watchdog reports a soft lockup.\n\nlnet_peer_needs_push() ignores FORCE_PUSH while PUSH_SENT is on.\nSo the discovery thread marks the peer discovered. It then resends\nthe pending messages of the peer. lnet_peer_is_uptodate_locked()\nchecks FORCE_PUSH directly. So each resend queues the message and\nthe peer again, and the discovery thread never sleeps.\n\nlnet_peer_is_uptodate_locked() now uses only lnet_peer_needs_push()\nfor FORCE_PUSH. The forced push goes after the ACK, as before.\n\nNew sanity-lnet test_244 makes this state on 2 nodes. It sends an\nlst RPC to the peer and checks the CPU time of lnet_discovery.\n\n    sanity-lnet test_244 on 2 tcp VMs\n    without the fix: 11 of 11 fail, 7 s of CPU in 7 s\n    with the fix:    0 of 32 fail, 0 s of CPU\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nFixes: 72726a311814 (\"LU-14810 lnet: Do not issue multiple PUSHes\")\nSigned-off-by: Chris Horn <chorn@ddn.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nChange-Id: Ia4ecaff1eea9404790b3206bc52ad5f34af9eb9f\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
